rooms_desc ({"You are magically transfered in the secret hideout of the Thief-legend Jrg.There are four possible ways to leave this room, but be careful if you arenot invited by the houseowner, for he may not like your being here.To the south you see a hallway full with trophies of the monsters, which Jrg has killed over the years of his thiefhood. To the west you see the shimmering and glittering of weapons he stole in his long legendary life. The room east of here is full of armours and other equipment to protect yourself against enemies. And finally to the north you see a corridor which ends at a door.","You just entered the hall of trophies. On the eastern and western wallsyou see the heads of many famous monsters. You recognize some of them as easy preys, but nevertheless you are very glad to know, that they cannotharm you anymore. Under each of these heads is a little sign, which tellsthe name of the monster and the date when Jrg had the pleasure to kill itthe first time. Some of these names sound familar to you, but others you never heard of.","You are inside Jrg's chamber of weaponry. You wonder where he got all thisstuff. The weapons are stored in display boxes or hang on the walls. You see swords, maces, knives, lances, staffs, axes, hammers, and a lot ofthings, that look like they weren't made by mortal hands.","This is the armoury, where all kind of protective devices, Jrg ever got inhis fingers, are stored. You see armours, cloaks, helmets, gloves, boots,rings, and amulets lying around in this tiny looking room. Some of theseitems emit a strange light, which let you come to the conclusion, that theywere either magical or not from this world.","You reached the end of Jrg's trophy hall. On these walls are the heads ofthe most fearsome monsters Jrg ever encountered. Even in death they lookvery dangerous indeed. The signs under these heads are different from thoseyou saw in the rest of the hallway. These signs are made of marble with theletters of pure gold. Jrg must have been very proud, that he spend so muchmoney on simple signs.","You reached to northern end of the hallway. To the north you see a hugeoaken door with a big sign on it.","This is Jrg's bureau, where he keeps track of his treasures and activitiesfor his guild. In the middle of the room stands a big wooden desk withhuge piles of paper on it. They are either new missions or letters fromhappy customers, who appreciate Jrg's good work.To the east you see some shimmering portals, the north room must be Jrg'sbedroom, and to the west you notice mountains of treasures.","Here are so much gold coins, that you think Jrg's must be the richest manin the entire world. He likes to count them, when he finds the time to do,but these days are hard, even for such a great thief like he is, and hehas one costumer after the other, so he keeps throwing in the coins in thisroom, without having the pleasure to count all of them, as he did when hewas an unknown but nevertheless successful Novice thief.","Many shimmering portals are gathered in this room and they all invite you toenter them, but where do they lead?","This is the mighty thief Jrg's private bedroom, where he like to take a napafter he had done some important work for his customers.",})
